  "workbook_description": [
    "ambr®250 data",
    "- each sheet contains data from one culture, with strain and condition indicated in the sheet name",
    "- duplicate cultures are numbered in brackets (1) or (2) - all (1) cultures were carried out at the same time and all (2) cultures at the same time, but (1) and (2) cultures not at the same time",
    "- values following YE or glucose (in sheet names) refer to the concentration of this ingredient in the medium or feed in g/L",
    "- two strains were included in these experiments: D-161646 and D-221704 (= T2). The strain is indicated in each sheet name, with D-221704 indicated as T2 (designation used in Vidgren et al. 2020) for easier reading",
    "- the volumes of acid added in the pH 3.5 and pH 3 cultures in the second set (2) are larger than those actually added (as obvious by visual inspection of the reactors), presumably because of air bubbles in the line",
    "- headings are those provided by the system, with extra text removed - the number in the heading refers to the vessel position in the ambr®250 system",
    "- offline data is provided in columns following the online data.",
    "- concentration of mucic acid includes that removed in samples",
    "- concentrations of mucic acid have been adjusted to take into account evaporation, as well as sample removal",
    "- evaporation was assessed by measuring the volume of each reactor at the end of the experiment and comparing with the volume calculated by ambr®250",
    "- a separate sheet gives the concentrations of substrate and co-substrate in the feed ",
    "- data published in Tamminen et al. 2022. AMB Express"
  ],
  "scope_limits": [
    "Dataset/schema and causal feature design selected after article reading and raw-field inspection, before any new model scoring. This is not a prospective blinded trial.",
    "Twenty real cultures belong to two shared experimental rounds and ten matched condition pairs. Vessels and shared feed bottles within a round are correlated; ten cultures are not ten independent experimental rounds.",
    "Round 1 to 2 is the prespecified primary direction; round 2 to 1 is only retrospective sensitivity. Both rounds share laboratory, apparatus, strains and recipe design; no new species/site/scale generalization.",
    "Online observation timestamps are treated as signal availability times. Raw signal arrival, preprocessing delays and assay-return logs are absent; this is conditional retrospective causal replay, not verified online deployment.",
    "No label interpolation. Offline initial samples without preceding online records are retained with an explicit exclusion; remaining observed samples need an online record no older than 0.5 h.",
